ths.ts, blob.ts, snippet.ts, normalize.ts (ByteBuilder, WsNormalizer, normalizeWS), grounding.ts (goUnquote, normalizedDiffSides, splitDiffByFile, newQuoteGrounder). - test/context/: helpers.ts (seeded rng, strings.Fields reference), paths, normalize, grounding, snippet, tree, hardening, bounds. ## Decisions / interpretations - \"Live guard blocks exactly what pinning leaves out\": compared over the fixture's file paths (blocked list, served list, .gitignore). A symlink (gitlink) is a 120000 blob in a plumbing-built capture, so directories/symlinks are excluded from that comparison; whether the snapshot keeps symlinks is ticket 22. - Diff header keys that are not valid UTF-8 are skipped (fail closed, change 24 spirit). goUnquote copies raw bytes >= 0x80 (Go would turn invalid ones into U+FFFD; such keys are skipped either way). - Parity kept: git appends a TAB to `---`/`+++` names containing a space; Go (and this port) then key the section as \"name\\t\", so such files never ground via the diff. Not fixed (not a listed deliberate change). - numberedSnippet rejects only on abort; everything else is a notice. - LineReader returns the line with its trailing `\\n` (Go readLineCapped); `eof` is true when the stream ended during that read. ## Progress All checklist items done; lint, typecheck, test:ts (1051) pass. ## 2026-11-18 12:26 -- ts-rewrite/14 attempt 1 -- done Effort: medium. Agent exit: 0. Subagents: 0. Cost: $5.75. Checked items: none. ### Agent notes # Ticket 14 notes (agent loop and token ledger) ## Seams - Ledger: unit (test/llm/ledger.ts). - Agent loop: runConversation / createClient driven by a scripted fake ModelClient (test/llm/agent-*.ts), injected now/sleep/sessionId. - [HTTP, chat] items: createClient over the real chat ModelClient and startInferenceServer. ## Progress All checklist items implemented and committed; lint, typecheck, test:ts (1904 assertions), go build, and npm test pass. ## Implemented - src/llm/ledger.ts (Ledger, newLedger, reserve, committed, weightedTokens; plus `outstanding()` for the mid-flight abort test). - src/llm/deadline.ts (WorkDeadline: check, callSignal, runTool). - src/llm/final-args.ts (parsePreservingIntegers, checkRequired, typeValidate, decodeArgs). - src/llm/retry.ts (withStepRetry, retryDelay, defaultSleep). - src/llm/messages.ts (transcriptBytes). - src/llm/review.ts (pure reviewResponse; returns stopCause {kind, text}). - src/llm/agent.ts (Conversation class + runConversation, constants). - src/llm/errors.ts: StopCauseKind, ErrorDetails.stopCause is now a kind, ErrorDetails.cause (cutoff cause text), cutoffError, FinalArgumentsError (precedence 2; no sentinel, Go parity). - src/llm/types.ts: TurnInfo, FinalSpec, ConverseOptions, RecordUsage, Client. - src/llm/client.ts: createClient; DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS now lives in agent.ts and is re-exported from client.ts. - Tests: test/llm/ledger.ts, agent-finalization.ts, agent-deadline.ts, agent-dispatch.ts, agent-http.ts, agent-helpers.ts (fake ModelClient); test/live/deepseek.ts + `npm run test:live`. ## Decisions / readings - TDD order: the ledger went strictly red -> green. The loop shell (agent.ts) is one tightly coupled unit, so it was written against spec 07 and Go agent.go first, then each checklist item got tests; I mutation-checked each group (removing block, bounds, buffered-abort guard, schema clone, sequential dispatch, abnormal-finish guard, etc.) and every mutation but one fails a test. The unobservable one: clearing `finalErr` on a provisional rejection -- in this design a non-null finalErr always stops the loop, so the clear cannot be seen. - Debug tracing (`roast:llm`) is NOT wired: AGENTS.md says no src module may import @substrate-system/debug until it passes the license allowlist. Add tracing when that is resolved. - \"Automatic tool choice\" at the fake seam is structural (ModelRequest has no tool-choice field; the chat encoder always sends \"auto\"); the HTTP test asserts body.tool_choice === \"auto\" on every re